\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. AND now, O Father, mindful of the love
\par That bought us, once for all, on Calvary's tree,
\par And having with us Him that pleads above,
\par We here present, we here spread forth to Thee
\par That only offering perfect in Thine eyes,
\par The one true, pure, immortal sacrifice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Look, Father, look on His annointed face,
\par And only look on us as found in Him;
\par Look not on our misusing of Thy grace,
\par Our prayer so languide, and our faith so dim:
\par For lo! between our sins and their reward
\par We set the passion of Thy Son our Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. And then for those, our dearest and our best,
\par By this prevailing presence we appeal;
\par O fold them closer to Thy mercy's breast,
\par O do Thine utmost for their souls true weal;
\par From tainting mischief keep them white and clear,
\par And crown Thy gifts with strength to persevere.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And so we come: O draw us to Thy feet,
\par Most patient Saviour, who canst love us still;
\par And by this food, so awful and so sweet,
\par Deliver us from every touch of ill:
\par In Thine own service make us glad and free,
\par And grant us never more to part with Thee.
\par                                       Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

